Description: Ask for high-priority EGL contexts for compositing
 Mir created its GL contexts with the default priority, so while a game kept
 the GPU busy (Potluck at 99% on the Radeon 8060S) every composite queued
 behind the game's frames and the whole desktop lagged: cursor, panel, dock
 and other windows. GNOME's and KDE's compositors ask for high priority
 (EGL_IMG_context_priority) for this. The gbm-kms and egl-generic rendering
 platforms and the cross-GPU copy surface now do too, through a header-only
 helper (no ABI change), falling back to a normal context when the extension
 is missing or the driver refuses: amdgpu and i915 give high priority only
 to the DRM master or a process with CAP_SYS_NICE, and Mir renders on the
 render node. The outcome is logged once ("EGL context priority: ...").
Author: Umoja developers
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-27
